    "done_when": "The re-profile at 7f9b87644 (~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/complete-reprofile.md) measured one warm promotion at 23.53 s, against an 81.86 s baseline. 16 to 20 s of it is the docs walk: reckon/_store.py:230 _resolve_html_file calls reckon/resources.py:544 resolve_resource 7 times, which makes 8 iter_resources scans and 651 uncached parse_meta parses. Each call walks the whole docs tree to find one slug. The node bounds this so one promotion walks each docs tree at most once. Either the scan is reused for an unchanged tree within the process, or the plan is resolved by its expected path, with the walk only as a fallback. Whatever it chooses must keep resolve_resource's guarantees: a duplicate live resource still raises ResourceCollision, an archived plan still resolves through the archive fallback, and a change to the tree between calls is seen. The node names its choice in the commit body. tests/test_a_promotion_walks_the_docs_tree_once.py counts iter_resources scans across the resolutions one promotion makes and asserts at most one per tree. It also asserts that a duplicate still raises, that an archived plan still resolves, and that a file added between two calls is found. Using the preserved scripts in /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261002T104603166755-crew-complete-time-after-the-bounds/complete-reprofile-artifacts/, the node re-runs the warm case on the fleet allocation and reports resolve_resource's cumulative time and call count beside 20.33 s / 8. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Base and head arms of every test file that imports reckon.resources or calls _resolve_html_file (found by grep at the base) show zero added failures, each log ending in its pytest summary and EXIT= line, run with -n 8.",
